\begin_layout Standard
Every chapter ends with a two-part problem section. Part I contains Core benchmarks to work without software: show the derivation, check feasibility or the defining identity, and state the economic point. Part II uses Proof and Applied problems as bridges to one named chapter case, which always appears last. Problem identifiers are stable across the book, course outline, and released handouts.
