Before using Codex, Python, or Lean, write four lines: Seed identifies the hand result being extended; Fixed records the assumptions that do not change; Scaled names the single enlarged dimension or strengthened claim; Risk states the new failure mode. A verified artifact must reproduce the seed, include a boundary or deliberately failing test, report the validation command, and separate the checked mathematical statement from the economic interpretation.
