\begin_layout Standard
The classical rational consumer chooses a feasible bundle to maximize a utility function.
  This chapter states that model,
 proves existence of demand,
 and develops its first-order characterization.
  Duality and welfare are treated in the next chapter.
 Throughout,
 
\begin_inset Formula $X=\mathbb{R}^{L}_{+}$
\end_inset

,
 
\begin_inset Formula $L\geq1$
\end_inset

 is the fixed number of commodities,
 
\begin_inset Formula $\notationfirst{price-domain}{\mathsf{P}}=\mathbb{R}^{L}_{++}$
\end_inset

,
 
\begin_inset Formula $\notationfirst{wealth-domain}{\mathsf{W}}=\mathbb{R}_{++}$
\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Note Note
status collapsed

