\begin_layout Section
Forecasting with Varian's Support Set
\end_layout

\begin_layout Definition
Given a finite price-choice dataset 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathcal{O}$
\end_inset

 and a new price-wealth pair 
\begin_inset Formula $(p^{T+1},w^{T+1})$
\end_inset

,
 define the augmented dataset associated with a candidate bundle by 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathcal{O}^{+}(x)=\mathcal{O}\cup\{(p^{T+1},x)\}$
\end_inset

.
 Varian's support set is 
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
\notationfirst{varian-support}{\mathcal{S}_{\mathcal{O}}(p^{T+1},w^{T+1})}=\left\{ x\in X:\begin{array}{l}
\mathcal{O}^{+}(x)\text{ satisfies GARP},\\
p^{T+1}\cdot x=w^{T+1}
\end{array}\right\} .
\]

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The definition already gives the exact criterion:
 a candidate bundle belongs to the support set if it exhausts the new budget and the augmented dataset satisfies GARP.
 The transitive closure must be checked,
 not only one-step comparisons.
 Whenever an old bundle 
\begin_inset Formula $x^{t}$
\end_inset

 is indirectly revealed preferred to the candidate,
 GARP requires the inequality 
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
p^{T+1}\cdot x\leq p^{T+1}\cdot x^{t}.
\]

\end_inset


\end_layout

