\begin_layout Standard
The exact-GARP tabulation in
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand citep
key "polissonquahrenou2020"
literal "false"

\end_inset

 reports that 12 of 47 participants in the symmetric treatment and 4 of 46 in the asymmetric treatment satisfy GARP.
 Overall,
 16 of 93 participants---approximately 17 percent---pass the exact test.
 The interpretation is precise but limited:
 a recorded panel that fails cannot be rationalized exactly by one locally nonsatiated utility function under the maintained budget data.
 The result alone does not distinguish preference instability from optimization error,
 recording error,
 or price misperception.
 Nor does a binary pass rate measure the economic magnitude of a violation:
 one strict revealed-preference cycle is sufficient for rejection.
 The critical cost-efficiency index introduced next provides a graded measure,
 while a random-choice benchmark helps assess the power of the design.
\end_layout

